<title>POLAND: POLISH SHARES CLOSE LOWER IN CONTINUOUS TRADE.</title>
<headline>POLISH SHARES CLOSE LOWER IN CONTINUOUS TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seven stocks fell, four rose and eight were flat in 19.6-million-zloty Warsaw bourse continuous trade on Wednesday with the WIG 20 index closing at 1,765.5 points, 1.7 percent lower than at the regular session.</p>
<p>The remaining three stocks did not trade.</p>
<p>NFI units fell 0.6 percent in a 25.5-million zloty-turnover.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
